A||||2||alpha||Has any one built an SCCA IT Fiero?||||1||
Z||000000||alpha||09-17-2000||05:51 PM||||I am just curious if anyone out there has built an SCCA Improved Touring Fiero...I have a couple questions just because I am interested...<P>1. Did you get a prefabricated roll cage (Can you even get one?) or did you make it yourself? Do use petty bars or cut the rear glass?<P>2. What suspension mods have you done?<P>3. Are brake mods allowed?<P>4. Is you are currently racing, is it competitive?<P>Thanks<P><BR>--Douglas Knight||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||09-18-2000||01:41 PM||||the shop that made my previous SE fast races a few SCCA IT (A & C) class cars as well as HSR and SVRA... Kirk Racing makes a full cage for our cars, so does Paeco in birmingham, al. the best suspension you can get would be stock front bar and addco rear, replace all the bushings with poly or delrin. konis, suspension tech, belltech or eibach springs, you CAN do up grades to the brakes.. but you can't make them bigger... you can vent them or slot them nautalis(sp) or x-drill them. if you go bigger you'll be in a different class... the regional 2nd place IT-A driver was able to make my car pull 1.14g where i could only muster about .96... yes it would be competative according to his lap times... but hes been driving for 15 years... <A HREF="http://www.scca.org" TARGET=_blank>www.scca.org</A>   <A HREF="http://www.kirkracing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.kirkracing.com</A>  <A HREF="http://www.racerwholesale.com" TARGET=_blank>www.racerwholesale.com</A> <P>(my se (currently owned by GT Bastard) was run at little talladega, Road Atlanta, and Roebling Road.. durning open track days when you don't need a liscence just a clue) <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 09-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||PJ||09-18-2000||08:33 PM||||alpha:<P>I've been racing an '88 GT since '93. The cage is from Al Kirk which is a showroom stock bolt-in design. Modified with welded in door bars (2 per side) and rear supports thru plexiglass to the strut towers. No Petty bar.<P>Suspension has poly bushings, shorter, stiffer springs and Koni's all around. The '88 suspension doesn't need a lot of tweaking. 225/50's on stock 15" wheels (with 3.94 final gear). I might go back to 205/50's on short twisty courses.<P>IT rotors and master cylinder must remain stock. No drilling or slotting. Ducting is allowed but not a must with the stock vented rotors. Pre '88 brakes need to be ducted. Prop. valve and flexible steel hose are OK. Pads & fluid unrestricted.<P>Competitiveness is much better since recently being reclassed a grade down from ITS to ITA.<BR>Not many cars can compete with the $40,000+ ready to race 2nd generation RX7's in ITS. Current hot cars in ITA are CRX's and Integra's. Haven't seen any well-sorted ITB 4 cyl. Fiero's yet.<P>PJ<BR>ITA #66 Black<BR> ||||reg||1
